<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Trump calls renewed Ukraine attacks on Russian oil refineries 'a disgrace'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4acb12a353a3d1b981cc65c89764f3b6558f83b8c9f3264c44cd5499b35e0051</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T01:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace--6cfecd7f8863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump called Ukraine's renewed strikes on Russian oil refineries a "disgrace" after Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky rejected his calls for an "energy ceasefire." Zelensky sought support from European allies earlier that day in Brussels on the sidelines of an EU summit. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>19 injured as minibus crashes into train at Channel Tunnel entrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80943c657620eb4a7209f93bf332cff23af6b4c36026978fa1a1376d83296e35</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance--79f37e5f8958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance" /><summary type="html">Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9932e54e1b7238077216ec1fec20f02e18d5e11d6d3b31a913e5fb5c551533d</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal--9bcf5af8133a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal" /><summary type="html">France and Germany have backed looser EU emissions rules for carmakers and agreed to include Britain in a “made in Europe” scheme, in a provisional deal reached Thursday that could reshape the bloc’s automotive and climate policies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecad6a43474593118a4a7fee40ec923122b35d863ad740564a13b5a400b9d030</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes--820569914737.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands, as tensions with Washington escalated over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8bbadd68c71d5bfae76df6e0b84b3c9007f742926a63476d5d98a14f2747899</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:45:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:03:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep--8a7157699d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep" /><summary type="html">Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613f6ff835a8d483ed9b70ddfb5218d28ce8984231d90047e15fc3d5f8a1ab16</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says--5033be605410.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".</summary></entry><entry><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1237d2218f9f968c4e6197b8e2eb5258f8940fe0e955e5b2f3a4683cbe0a671c</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:04:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--33513f001314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Albania's leader defies calls to resign as student protesters rampage in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8f4a896d80ec6704a111b2aa2a0c1d1beb088f668ae5b5796f5627d4db7b98</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:02:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital--247a1ee2a654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital" /><summary type="html">​Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Thursday rejected calls to resign as thousands of student-led protesters smashed windows and fought running battles with riot police firing water cannon and tear gas in the capital. The demonstrators accuse officials of corruption and neglecting education and say they are angry about the sale of parts of Albania's southern coastline to a luxury resort development backed ​by US President ‌Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Trump really pull the plug? Starlink restored but Ukraine's fate still uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76d2c762c66c9998eadc61a5d30bb3f38298057047c0209fec9627aebc0c3863</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:38:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain--2088cc5dba32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain" /><summary type="html">Can a flick of a switch really be enough for Donald Trump and Elon Musk to end Ukraine's hopes of holding out against Russia? With Kyiv already reeling from daily strikes by Russia's new motor-powered drones, the United States decision to slow SpaceX Starlink service felt immediately Wednesday when air raid warnings failed.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3facbc66c6079a76d9b3b92f81b8a84f65a4fa12810a95e5339c6e539661cc11</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms--b38db7502a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37bb3009e41f49dbe2c9ce52dd3ce476adc05df9dbff3490e5b0fff935e113a0</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:14:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-tal--b4d9641c071b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.</summary></entry><entry><title>NATO to address drone attacks in the Black Sea after seven missing off Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2e0e264a1b3a8e54b1a070215e9c1176aea6d49a73220b00ac980a88e38710a</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--d31e01c8ba8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">NATO will put drone strikes in the Black Sea on its agenda at a meeting next week, officials said Thursday, following two new attacks and the disappearance of seven people. Incidents involving civilian vessels in the Black Sea have been on the rise off the coasts of Bulgaria and Romania in a suspected spillover from Russia’s war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Student protests spread in Albania as demonstrators call for PM resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8be2a760b78a04b809289c875b23186d69d2ea149a0a7109aae4108825b5a76</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:27:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation--ceb6c228c280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation" /><summary type="html">Clashes broke out between demonstrators and police for the third consecutive day on Thursday in Albania, with Prime Minister Edi Rama condemning the “chaos” that caused damage to government buildings. Thousands of protesters are calling for Rama's resignation and better studying conditions for Albanian students.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia detains independent outlet Novaya Gazeta editor Sergei Sokolov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f072f90ce6532850dd343f6282fa1dfbb3bb6f184f93d21423bd8711a0f5730e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T11:39:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search--614591d58672.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search" /><summary type="html">Sergei Sokolov, the editor-in-chief of Russia's independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, was detained and taken for questioning on Thursday after authorities searched his home, the newspaper said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'American abandonment' threatens Ukraine's civilians in war against Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f38540e52dbc32034f9e48e7597272cb401184790ba0d66d2238acb16cad7200</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T11:09:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia--f328a2383f92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 15: First, reported Starlink disruptions in Ukraine make the European front pages. Next, US papers go into more detail about the situation. Also, an unusual alliance forms in Germany between far-right and far-left parties. Meanwhile, the winners of the Wildlife Photographer of the Year awards have been announced. Finally, Finland flaunts its smelly islands.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>War in Ukraine: Kyiv residents decry shortage of bomb shelters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa2a1ed9171eea04d436c2a07da15942eb14344321a264a1850086a0d24070f5</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T09:50:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261015-war-in-ukraine-kyiv-residents-decry-shortage-of-bomb-shelters--24e14b727432.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261015-war-in-ukraine-kyiv-residents-decry-shortage-of-bomb-shelters" /><summary type="html">Kyiv's mayor, Vitaly Klitschko, has advised those residents who can "temporarily relocate" for the winter to do so. That advice has been met with derision at best from many residents, who say his administration is responsible for failing to better prepare the Ukrainian capital for Russian attacks. In particular, they complain of a severe shortage of adequate bomb shelters.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders head into high-stakes budget battle as elections loom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bfb4712ac7522d531ba7410abbd94cd9a27353286b7f21d858e964da60ed15f</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T06:03:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-leaders-head-into-high-stakes-budget-battle-as-elections-loom--e828309e2bd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-leaders-head-into-high-stakes-budget-battle-as-elections-loom" /><summary type="html">EU leaders head to a summit on Thursday seeking a deal on the bloc’s nearly €2 trillion budget for 2028-2034 by Christmas amid deep divisions over spending and fears that upcoming elections, particularly in France, could strengthen eurosceptic forces.</summary></entry><entry><title>France 'can no longer finance' Ukraine, far-right presidential frontrunner Le Pen says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38cd6b600ce0ae559278b0778d05a906b0c79b46a86216987890fb1f71a97cb9</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T05:49:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-can-no-longer-finance-ukraine-far-right-candidate-marine-le-pen-says--1262c2d6cd2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-can-no-longer-finance-ukraine-far-right-candidate-marine-le-pen-says" /><summary type="html">Far-right leader and presidential candidate Marine Le Pen said on Wednesday that France could no longer afford to fund Ukraine, citing the country's high deficit and weak economic growth.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky meets NATO chief and EU leaders in push to apply 'real pressure' on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6002d68aa1cde4da2c1a542d8fe5587731fedc18bc228fb0cbb3817fd601b8a0</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T03:52:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker--ecf4ed2542dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky arrived in Brussels Thursday to rally support at a meeting with NATO chief Mark Rutte the same day, and a summit with EU leaders to follow Friday. Earlier, Zelensky asked the United States not to stand with Moscow and called for "honesty" after Kyiv said it had been betrayed by Washington's intelligence-sharing gaps. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges EU to agree to long-term budget by Christmas ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2f92018e82eb1dbb1e4c526c16968df55f1f17908c56813c923447806e8b6a4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T01:59:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-eu-leaders-head-for-showdown-over-bloc-budget--bbe5af08a60f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-eu-leaders-head-for-showdown-over-bloc-budget" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron urged EU leaders on Thursday to reach a deal on the bloc’s nearly €2 trillion budget by Christmas, warning that elections in France and other European countries in 2027 could leave little room for compromise as divisions deepen over spending priorities and funding.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Albania protests turn violent as protestors demand PM Rama's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca146e35844905be07e540e31bd3e6d440435682cd9df797b18b17c82a70e46b</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T22:35:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation--fc3550df0859.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation" /><summary type="html">Anti-government protests in Albania’s capital Tirana turned violent for a second consecutive night on Wednesday, leaving several government buildings damaged and at least one ablaze. As thousands demanded improved university conditions and the government's resignation, Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama said he would not step down.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b9d9366d7d05527a8a089292a1df115a607dbdc188fe1ebc0a6b7c49447ae62</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting--965e949188ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".</summary></entry><entry><title>What is Starshield, SpaceX's military version of Starlink?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:248f7f7f316eb01c318d5287dd51ab3102289558d94528f4f2a6b0b07653fadd</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:15:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink--420f2336136c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk’s ⁠SpaceX restricted “military-grade” ​Starlink services overnight into Wednesday, hampering Ukrainian drone strike missions and air defences, Ukraine reported. In response, Musk said that the US government was behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78d698e21566cf7aae438399aa003710ec0c2570d9f533a99def50173e5b259e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing--ce42ad081609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing" /><summary type="html">Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c11575afdb81b30f36811be31d695b3c5dfc8c1d63d03b3995860236b1742f2a</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres--fd09c9bb9e0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far".</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b488f6ef0d4f09e558ebfd9e035faebd22f60beb4d442d0c050997be5295ae75</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions--3220e9df249a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'massive' oil, gas and mineral exploration to begin in Greenland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b913f2686816596d1fb34034f1c6d382f49e71144295856adfde01399b954b4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:41:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland--f4d2d91425e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said on Wednesday that a "massive" oil, gas and mineral exploration was slated to begin in Greenland. The US, Denmark and Greenland last month signed a security agreement after Trump's repeated threats to seize control of the island.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trial lawyer for Ukrainian accused of sabotage says Russia used Nord Stream as a ‘weapon’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cf305a2b555c896fbd7c168122ab5073aabbe74164add43de86a91abe4558ba</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:37:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-defence-of-ukrainian-accused-of-sabotage-says-russia-used-nord-stream-pipelines-as-weapon--ab78193a18b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-defence-of-ukrainian-accused-of-sabotage-says-russia-used-nord-stream-pipelines-as-weapon" /><summary type="html">The Nord Stream gas pipelines were a political and economic “weapon” for Russia, the lawyer for former Ukrainian officer Sergei Kuznetsov said Wednesday. The first to appear in the high-profile case, Kuznetsov is accused by German prosecutors of having led the plan to sabotage the infrastructure in 2022.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US government behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system, Musk says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b71ba6dd40b2822730fd1a480d201c8cf51b923145b965f22e40c12a49207b1e</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:19:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead--c9372a6d0ab2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead" /><summary type="html">SpaceX boss Elon Musk said Wednesday that any disruptions in the Starshield satellite communications system would be the responsibility of the US government, not his company. Earlier, Ukraine’s President Volodymyr Zelensky called on Musk to “switch on” the system which Kyiv relies on for communications and logistics. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about Pope Leo XIV's lung cancer diagnosis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b8e2f99cf424ffc4991e33b2aabb91ed77a7eff6fad3453a3209027a7a47a9</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:35:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation--ea1d8bfcf529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo underwent surgery on Tuesday to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung after saying that a nodule had been "detected at a very early stage". Following a "successful" operation, the Vatican said the 71-year-old pontiff would undergo additional testing.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
